    <div class="col-lg-9">
        <section id="staff-login" class="help-section">
            <h2>Sign in (staff)</h2>
            <p>Go to <a href="/login">/login</a>. MET Electrical office sign-in is <code>admin@met.demo</code> / <code>Demo123!</code>. If your company connected Google, Microsoft, or X, use those buttons — we only sign in emails that already have a METERP account (an administrator must create you first).</p>
            <p>Accounts with authenticator 2FA will ask for a 6-digit code after the password. Customers use <a href="/portal/login">/portal/login</a>, not this screen.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="cash-desk" class="help-section">
            <h2>Home cash desk</h2>
            <p>After login, Home is the daily queue: approve quotes/requisitions/leave/field reports, send approved quotes, convert won work to jobs, raise deposit invoices, chase overdue invoices, record remaining payment, receive late POs, and return outstanding PPE. One click per row. Confirm dialogs always ask before money or stock moves.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="cash-rules" class="help-section" data-testid="help-cash-rules">
            <h2>Cash desk rules</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Quotes.</strong> Tick Includes VAT to type the gross figure: at 15%, R 115.00 stores ex-VAT R 100.00 and VAT R 15.00, and travel uses the same tick. The register From and To include those days, and the VAT column is the tax stored on the quote.</li>
                <li><strong>Quote print.</strong> The printed quote shows our VAT number and the customer VAT number when both are set. A blank customer VAT number is left off, and the quote still prints.</li>
                <li><strong>Quote to job.</strong> Converting a quote sets the job quoted total to the VAT-inclusive quote total once, travel stays a job cost, and converting the same quote again is refused.</li>
                <li><strong>Customers.</strong> Payment terms (days) sets the invoice due date (blank or 0 stays 30 days), and search matches the VAT number as well as the name, email, and phone. On the account statement, Export CSV uses the lines on the screen and the last balance is the closing balance; draft, proforma, and cancelled documents stay off it.</li>
                <li><strong>Invoices.</strong> Issue credit note on a draft so the VAT-inclusive credit reduces what the customer owes; a credit left in Draft does not. Credit this amount credits a VAT-inclusive part that cannot exceed the balance due and needs a reason, while Create credit note still credits the whole invoice.</li>
                <li><strong>Customers in credit.</strong> On Invoices, customers whose open credit notes exceed open invoices show in credit and are left off the overdue list. Draft credits are left out.</li>
                <li><strong>Receipts.</strong> On Invoices, Allocate one receipt splits one EFT across that customer's open invoices, the amounts must add up to the bank amount, and draft, proforma, cancelled, and credit notes are left off. Reverse needs a reason and puts the receipt back on the balance, and a receipt cannot be reversed twice.</li>
                <li><strong>Deposit.</strong> On Command Center, issuing a full credit of the only deposit clears the deposit flag while the job is still open, and a partial credit that still covers the deposit does not. Reversing a deposit receipt clears that flag only when the deposit is no longer fully paid and no other deposit still covers it; a closed job is left unchanged.</li>
                <li><strong>Chase.</strong> Chasing an overdue invoice states the net still owed after receipts and open credit notes. A paid invoice, or one already covered by credit, is not chased.</li>
                <li><strong>Command Center.</strong> The job card shows TRFid, job card number, team, region, and customer order, and a missing value is a dash. The customer order number saves on the job; blank stays empty and does not change quote or invoice totals.</li>
                <li><strong>Inventory.</strong> The register shows on hand, reorder level, and shortfall. Inactive items stay off the list.</li>
                <li><strong>Purchase orders.</strong> On Purchase orders, Still to receive lists open lines with ordered, received, and outstanding. Fully received and cancelled orders are left off.</li>
                <li><strong>Goods received.</strong> On GRV Register, the delivery note saved with the goods receipt is shown. A GRV with no note shows a dash.</li>
                <li><strong>Payroll.</strong> On Payroll, the weekly timesheet is Monday to Sunday, hours sit on the posted day, and closed-job hours stay. The total equals the cells.</li>
                <li><strong>Portal.</strong> On the customer portal, the outstanding balance matches that customer's statement as at today.</li>
                <li><strong>Finance.</strong> Output VAT uses the tax already stored, credit notes reduce the total, and the CSV total matches the screen. Draft, proforma, and cancelled documents are left out.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section id="quotes" class="help-section">
            <h2>Quotes</h2>
            <ol>
                <li>Open <strong>Quotes</strong> → New Quote (or <code>/quotes?create=1</code>).</li>
                <li>Pick a customer or create one on the form.</li>
                <li>Add lines: labour, materials, and a separate <strong>Travel</strong> line. Unit cost + GP% sets sell price.</li>
                <li>Save, submit for executive approval, then <strong>Sent</strong> (approval is required before send).</li>
                <li>When the customer accepts, convert to a job (or sales order first). Travel copies onto the job.</li>
            </ol>
        </section>
        <section id="jobs" class="help-section">
            <h2>Jobs &amp; Command Center</h2>
            <p>Open a job at <code>/jobs/&#123;id&#125;</code>. Capture labour, material costs, field reports, and travel until the job is <strong>Closed</strong>. Raising an invoice does <em>not</em> close the job. Close is an executive P&amp;L review: Approve close → hard lock. Reopen needs an executive reason and is audited.</p>
            <p>Work sign-off (manager → executive) is separate from close. Emergency jobs can start without a quote.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="stock" class="help-section">
            <h2>Stock, purchase orders, PPE</h2>
            <p>Field techs submit requisitions from the field portal. Managers then executives approve. Catalog lines reserve stock; shortfall goes to procurement → PO → GRV (goods receipt) → issue to the job. Non-catalog (free-text) lines always go to procurement. PPE is issued to an <strong>employee</strong>; job is optional. Return PPE from Home or the PPE register — stock is restocked.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="invoices" class="help-section">
            <h2>Invoices, payments, Sage &amp; Xero</h2>
            <p>Create deposit / progress / final invoices from Command Center or Home while the job is open. Record payments (POP download when attached). Open a customer for the account statement: invoices, credit notes, and receipts, with a VAT-inclusive balance. Draft, proforma, and cancelled documents are left off. On <strong>Finance</strong>, choose Sage or Xero and export a sales CSV your bookkeeper can import. The same page has <strong>Output VAT</strong> for a date range: stored tax, credit notes reduce the total, and the CSV total matches the screen. If the tenant has an invoice webhook URL, sent invoices are also posted there as JSON.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Sage</strong> — sales daybook CSV (type, account, date, reference, net/VAT/gross).</li>
                <li><strong>Xero</strong> — official sales invoice import columns (contact, invoice number, dates, qty, unit amount, tax type, ZAR).</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section id="portal" class="help-section">
            <h2>Customer portal</h2>
            <p>Customers sign in at <a href="/portal/login">/portal/login</a> with the email on their customer record. They see only their quotes and invoices. On the customer portal, the outstanding balance matches that customer's statement as at today. They can <strong>Accept</strong> a sent quote and send an <strong>I've paid</strong> notice (the office still records the receipt). They cannot see jobs, stock, or other customers. Office staff create portal users from Users (tick “Customer portal login” and pick the customer). MET demo: <code>portal@met.demo</code> / <code>Demo123!</code>, linked to a MET customer.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="grok" class="help-section">
            <h2>Grok Bot (AI copilot)</h2>
            <p>Open <strong>AI Copilot</strong> (sparkle button) or <a href="/ai-copilot">/ai-copilot</a>. Ask in plain language: “create a quote with travel for Kruger Park Lodge”, “why is this job over budget?”, “what is low in stock?”. Apply suggestions onto a real quote or job, then download the PDF.</p>
            <p>To use <strong>your own Grok / Gemini / OpenAI subscription</strong>: go to <a href="/settings/ai">AI Settings</a> (tenant managers). Click <strong>Continue with Grok</strong> (or Google / OpenAI), sign in at the provider console, paste the API key, and save. Keys are encrypted at rest. Platform <code>XAI_API_KEY</code> / <code>Ai__ApiKey</code> is used when tenant override is off.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="ai" class="help-section" data-testid="help-ai-key">
            <h2>AI key (Copilot)</h2>
            <p>Copilot at <a href="/ai-copilot">/ai-copilot</a> calls a live model only when a key is configured. A blank <code>Ai:ApiKey</code> is not a key. Paste one on <a href="/settings/ai">AI Settings</a>, Save, then Test connection. The same page masks a saved tenant key.</p>
            <p>Deployment names (no values in source control): <code>Ai:ApiKey</code>, <code>Ai:BaseUrl</code>, <code>Ai:Model</code>, <code>Ai:Provider</code>, <code>Ai:Enabled</code>. Environment equivalents use a double underscore (<code>Ai__ApiKey</code>). <code>XAI_API_KEY</code> is also read when the config key is empty. Default provider is Grok at <code>https://api.x.ai/v1</code>, model <code>grok-4.6</code>.</p>
            <p>Ask with a TRFid such as FT16010, SD393, or PD0085. Travel stays an explicit line. An invoice does not close the job.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="field" class="help-section">
            <h2>Field technicians</h2>
            <p>Field users land on <a href="/field">/field</a>: jobs, stock requisitions, leave, field reports. They are denied office modules (finance, users, AI settings). Submit reports with real content; closed jobs reject new reports.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="help-section">
            <h2>Roles at a glance</h2>
            <table class="table">
                <thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>Where</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Executive / Admin</td><td>Home, Approvals, Command Center</td><td>Approve, send, invoice, close jobs, AI settings, Sage/Xero export</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Manager</td><td>Approvals, Jobs</td><td>First-pass approvals, labour, costs</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Technician</td><td>/field</td><td>Reports, stock REQ, leave</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Customer</td><td>/portal</td><td>Own quotes and invoices only</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>
